      "dedupe_key": "architecture-on-stage-walters-cohen|2026-10-22|barbican",
      "description": "Discover the projects and ideas behind Walters & Cohen's thoughtful, people-focused architecture. Founded in 1994 by Cindy Walters and Michál Cohen, their work places particular emphasis on creating inclusive, sustainable and enduring spaces that respond carefully to their surroundings. Notable projects include the Dorothy Garrod Building at Newnham College, Cambridge, and the Vajrasana Buddhist Retreat Centre in Suffolk. The practice has also developed an estates strategy for Murray Edwards College, Cambridge, helping shape the long-term future of its Grade II* listed Chamberlin, Powell and Bon campus.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/event_listing_small_jpg/public/images/2026-09/Godolphin%20and%20Latymer%20School-Jim%20Stephenson.jpg?itok=UjvPO5d5",
      "lat": 51.5201,
      "lng": -0.0955,
      "price": {
