      "date_text": "Thu 22 Oct 2026, 19:00",
      "description": "\n  <p>Discover the projects and ideas behind Walters &amp; Cohen's thoughtful, people-focused architecture.</p>\n\n<p>Founded in 1994 by <strong>Cindy Walters</strong> and <strong>Michál Cohen</strong>, their work places particular emphasis on creating inclusive, sustainable and enduring spaces that respond carefully to their surroundings.&nbsp;</p><p>Notable projects include the Dorothy Garrod Building at Newnham College, Cambridge, and the Vajrasana Buddhist Retreat Centre in Suffolk.&nbsp;</p><p>The practice has also developed an estates strategy for Murray Edwards College, Cambridge, helping shape the long-term future of its Grade II* listed Chamberlin, Powell and Bon campus.</p>",
      "ends": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/event_listing_small_jpg/public/images/2026-09/Godolphin%20and%20Latymer%20School-Jim%20Stephenson.jpg?itok=UjvPO5d5",
