      ],
      "date_text": "Mon 2 — Mon 9 Nov 2026",
      "description": "\n  <p><span>Italian comedy meets American satire. Two marriages, two worlds — one unmissable evening.</span></p>\n\n<p>At first glance, <strong>Gian Carlo Menotti</strong>'s sparkling comic opera <em><strong>Amelia al ballo</strong></em><strong> </strong>and <strong>Leonard Bernstein</strong>'s jazz-inflected <em><strong>Trouble in Tahiti</strong></em><strong> </strong>could not be more different. Look closer, and they are in illuminating conversation.</p><p>Both centre on compelling female protagonists whose desires are constrained by the marriages meant to sustain them, offering a revealing portrait of two Western cultures at a 20th-century crossroads.</p><p>The UK premiere of <em>Amelia al ballo</em> follows the irrepressible Amelia as she outwits a suspicious husband and needy lover to attend the season's grandest ball.&nbsp;</p><p>In <em>Trouble in Tahiti</em>, Dinah and Sam's seemingly perfect suburban life masks deep unhappiness, exposing the cracks beneath the American dream.&nbsp;</p><p>Directed by <strong>Ashley Dean</strong>, this new double-bill production is set in the 1950s.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.guildhall-programmes.co.uk/double-bill-2026\"><strong>Please explore the free digital programme.&nbsp;</strong></a></p>",
      "ends": "2026-11-09T19:00:00Z",
      "image_url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/sites/default/files/styles/event_listing_small_jpg/public/images/2026-07/2026_Autumn_Season_digital%20assets_Opera_1920x1080px_no%20text.jpg?itok=uI30IV6d",
      "listing_title": "Double Bill: Amelia al ballo & Trouble in Tahiti",
      "price_text": "£30",
      "room": "Silk Street Theatre",
      "series": [],
      "starts": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z",
      "subtitle": "Amelia al ballo & Trouble in Tahiti",
      "title": "Guildhall Opera Double Bill",
      "url": "https://www.barbican.org.uk/whats-on/2026/event/double-bill-amelia-al-ballo-trouble-in-tahiti"
    }
  },
