      "date_text": "Thu 19 Nov 2026, 19:30",
      "description": "\n  <p><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The saxophonist, rapper and composer Soweto Kinch revisits the trilogy of works he has created with LSO since 2019, with music from </span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">The Black Peril</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">, </span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">White Juju</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> and </span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Soundtrack to the Apocalypse</span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">. </span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Each work was inspired by a panoply of events, from commemorating the race riots of 1919 to the intensely fought culture wars in 2020 and lockdown, and the emergence of an apocalyptic, post-truth world. Covering Past, Present and Future</span><em><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> </span></em><span lang=\"EN-GB\">they break beyond the boundaries of genre to explore these resonant themes. The layered storytelling, lyricism and musicality deliberately upends conventions – its often challenging messages are even more salient today. </span><span>&nbsp;</span></p><p><span lang=\"EN-GB\">In Soweto’s words, ‘I’ve been on an intense journey, playing with and subverting tropes, gaining confidence in my own compositional voice but also discovering new approaches to storytelling with each commission.’ The results are this mix of cerebral and guttural, danceable creations – multi-platform works which should ‘assail the senses, but enrich the soul’.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>",
      "ends": null,
